  "historical_remaining_before_native_rust_v1": [
    "Reconcile all selected v1.4.7 native failure/type/error wrapping and NewWatcher/Add/Close ordering. Linux uses nonblocking AsyncFd rather than the source blocking inotify+poller allocation sequence; Windows uses event/wait completion rather than source IOCP.",
    "Reconcile BSD source 100ms timed kevent/done/Close schedules versus cancellable readiness, close errors/nonblocking error delivery, partial initialization races, and existing-watch register failure with retained stale fd numbers. Native ownership never creates a second OwnedFd for a reused stale number.",
    "Reconcile exact Windows filepath.Clean/UTF16/long-name/case/normalization, source MAX_PATH and malformed record, access/attribute and kernel-error/partial-buffer profiles. The adapter serves Agones single-path Watch; arbitrary vendor multi-Add/Remove APIs are not a separate utility contract.",
    "Final Windows console-hook removal/wait unregister or undrainable filesystem I/O still has an explicit unverified abort policy; emergency Drop can block. Actual M0027 process exit and interaction with preserved old handlers remain required.",
    "Enumerate any required source build-tag/platform configurations outside the authored Unix/Windows branches before a platform acceptance claim. Source-declared Solaris failure is preserved; modern fsnotify FEN behavior is not substituted.",
    "All other M0003 HTTP/TLS/gateway/queue/config/CRD/logging/feature/admission profiles, source-body reconciliation and caller adoption remain required. No platform completion, assurance or route-switch credit follows from this authoring."
  ],
  "historical_signals_before_tokio_adoption": {
    "authored_operations": [
      "Common CGP SourceSignalSubscriber path owns one hub/session, subscription ids, one-slot source channels, weak registrations, parent child token and reader spawn/rejection cleanup on Unix and Windows",
      "Windows SetConsoleCtrlHandler lease with exclusive process claim, atomic pending/waker bridge, active-callback quiescence and explicit removal; stale readers cannot poll or fan out through a replacement lease",
      "CTRL_C and CTRL_BREAK deliver source SIGINT; CLOSE/LOGOFF/SHUTDOWN deliver source SIGTERM and park the OS-created callback thread as the source runtime does",
      "Window terminal parking holds no Rust lease/task/waker/context; actual parent cleanup/process exit remains the M0027 owner. Stop removes future notifications without joining an OS-owned terminal callback",
      "Both explicit Stop and owner close restore/remove the selected hook; reader Drop/rejected spawn cleans the same lease. Final failed restoration abort is an explicit native failure policy, not source parity credit"
    ],
